From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:43:30 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] scsi: ufs: preserve unsupported sense for blocked
 discard operations

Keep DATA_PROTECT for denied WRITE(10/16) ranges so SCSI does not downgrade the entire LUN. Report ILLEGAL_REQUEST for other denied commands so sd disables unsupported UNMAP and WRITE SAME operations. The write allow-list is unchanged.

Change-Id: Ic6ef406e065b77552068676a60d83e73315391de
---
 drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
index 0a4333274..1e775cb43 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -3298,8 +3298,12 @@ static int ufshcd_queuecommand(struct Scsi_Host *host, struct scsi_cmnd *cmd)
 	    !a50_ufs_write_allowed(cmd->device->lun, cmd->cmnd, A50_UD_FIRST, A50_UD_LAST)) {
 		dev_warn_ratelimited(hba->dev, "A50_UFS_SAFE: blocked SCSI opcode 0x%02x lun %llu\n",
 				     cmd->cmnd[0], cmd->device->lun);
-		/* Policy denial, not an unsupported opcode: keep SCSI on WRITE(10). */
-		scsi_build_sense(cmd, 0, DATA_PROTECT, 0x27, 0);
+		/* Denied ranges must not disable WRITE(10) for the whole LUN. */
+		if (cmd->cmnd[0] == WRITE_10 || cmd->cmnd[0] == WRITE_16)
+			scsi_build_sense(cmd, 0, DATA_PROTECT, 0x27, 0);
+		else
+			/* Let sd disable unsupported UNMAP/WRITE SAME operations. */
+			scsi_build_sense(cmd, 0, ILLEGAL_REQUEST, 0x20, 0);
 		scsi_done(cmd);
 		return 0;
 	}
